  "narration": [
    {
      "t": 0.5,
      "text": "Every merge prints a fingerprint. Here is how you carry one forward into the next merge."
    },
    {
      "t": 4.8,
      "text": "Two layers, already in the order we want them."
    },
    {
      "t": 10.8,
      "text": "Merge them, and look at the middle line. That fingerprint is the thing we want to keep."
    },
    {
      "t": 16.8,
      "text": "So we stage it into a layer of its own, in the usual order for this tool. Watch what I type."
    },
    {
      "t": 22.8,
      "text": "There it is, stored under a name of our choosing."
    },
    {
      "t": 28.8,
      "text": "A layer that is not in the order contributes nothing at all, so we add it."
    },
    {
      "t": 34.8,
      "text": "And merge again. Notice this merge reports a different fingerprint from the first one."
    },
    {
      "t": 40.8,
      "text": "The file carries the earlier fingerprint, which is the one we pinned, not this merge's own."
    },
    {
      "t": 44.5,
      "text": "Carry what the first merge printed into a layer of its own, add it to the order, and merge again."
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Teaches that the fingerprint is only available from the merge output, that it is carried as a value, and that the second merge has a different fingerprint."
}
